  <h2>You should know how to leave before you sign up</h2>
  <p>Dark-pattern cancellations are endemic in subscription products. Chat platforms are no exception. Common tactics:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Requiring cancellation through email support with a 48-hour response window.</li>
    <li>Hiding the cancellation page behind account settings that are not linked from the billing page.</li>
    <li>Offering a "pause" instead of a "cancel" button.</li>
    <li>Continuing to bill after cancellation with a "processing period" explanation.</li>
    <li>Refusing prorated refunds even when cancellation occurs minutes after renewal.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We test every product's cancellation flow and report what actually happens — not what the terms page promises.</p>
  <h2>What we test</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Account creation:</strong> Sign up with a real payment method.</li>
    <li><strong>Subscription purchase:</strong> Buy the lowest-tier paid plan.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancellation attempt:</strong> Find and complete the cancellation flow. Record the number of clicks and screens required.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirmation:</strong> Verify cancellation is confirmed in writing (email or in-app).</li>
    <li><strong>Refund request:</strong> If a refund is offered, request it and record the outcome.</li>
    <li><strong>Account deletion:</strong> Request full account and data deletion. Verify through a follow-up login attempt.</li>
    <li><strong>Rebill check:</strong> Monitor the payment method for 30 days for unexpected charges.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Scoring</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Excellent:</strong> One-click cancellation from the billing page, instant confirmation, prorated refund offered, account deletion completed within 48 hours.</li>
    <li><strong>Good:</strong> Cancellation requires 2–3 clicks, confirmation within minutes, deletion available but may take up to a week.</li>
    <li><strong>Poor:</strong> Cancellation requires contacting support, hidden cancellation page, no prorated refund, account deletion unavailable or ignored.</li>
    <li><strong>Fail:</strong> Cannot cancel without disputing the charge; continued billing after cancellation; account deletion refused.</li>
  </ul>
